@*
    The `CodeBlock` the UI design mandates for the parity-compare output (REQ-UI-033).

    TR-003 is CLOSED — `TrBlazeUI.Components.CodeBlock.CodeBlock` ships in 2.1.0-ci.10 — and this
    component is KEPT anyway, deliberately, because the shipped one does not draw what
    `docs/mockups/export.html` draws. Two differences, checked against the shipped component rather
    than assumed:

      • Its copy affordance is a TEXT button reading `Copy` / `Copied` (`h-6 px-2 text-xs`). The
        mockup's `.codeblk .cb-h` puts a ghost ICON button carrying `#i-copy` there, and the mockup
        -parity gate reads control shape off exactly that element.
      • Its bar label is the `Language` parameter — a language tag. The label this block carries is a
        title, `parity-compare output`, and passing a sentence as a language would be a misuse that
        the next reader has to unpick.

    Everything else about the shipped component matches (bordered rounded box, mono label bar,
    horizontally scrolling `<pre><code>` body), so this is a two-line gap, not a rewrite. Swapping
    would trade a documented mockup match for a deletion, which is the wrong trade. Revisit when
    `CodeBlock` grows a title slot or an icon-only copy control.

    The body scrolls inside itself so a long compare line can never widen the page.
*@
@namespace TfLens.Components.Pages.ExportParts
@inject IJSRuntime objJsRuntime
@inject ToastService objToastService

<div class="tflens-codeblock" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">
    <div class="tflens-codeblock-bar">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">@Title</span>
        <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                Size="ButtonSize.IconSmall"
                AriaLabel="@($"Copy {Title}")"
                OnClick="CopyAsync">
            <LucideIcon Name="copy" Size="14" />
        </Button>
    </div>
    <pre class="tflens-codeblock-body"><code>@Code</code></pre>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The label shown in the block's bar.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Title { get; set; } = "output";

    /// <summary>The text rendered verbatim inside the block.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Code { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Anything else the caller sets — <c>data-testid</c> above all — lands on the block.</summary>
    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Copies the block's text to the clipboard.
    /// </summary>
    /// <returns>A task that completes once the outcome has been reported to the user.</returns>
    private async Task CopyAsync()
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(Code))
        {
            return;
        }

        var vCopied = await objJsRuntime.InvokeAsync<bool>("tflens.copyText", Code);

        if (vCopied)
        {
            objToastService.Success($"{Title} copied to the clipboard.", "Copied");
        }
        else
        {
            objToastService.Error("The browser refused clipboard access.", "Couldn't copy");
        }
    }
}
